{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}EU grid registers we read — {{ SITE }}{% endblock %}
{% block main %}
<h1>EU grid registers we read</h1>
<p>Grid operators in several EU countries publish lists of inverters, batteries and chargers that meet their connection rules.
None of them links to the others. We read five and show, per model, which of them list it — with a link back, because the register is the authority.</p>
<div class="rows">
{% for k, r in registers.items() %}
<article class="row"><h3>{{ k }} — <a href="{{ r.url }}">{{ r.name }}</a></h3>
<dl><dt>Snapshot</dt><dd>{{ r.snapshot }}</dd></dl></article>
{% endfor %}
</div>
<h2>Not used</h2>
<ul class="prose">
  <li><strong>Belgium (Synergrid C10/26)</strong> — the list is public, but its terms allow personal use only. Check it yourself at
  <a href="https://www.synergrid.be/">synergrid.be</a>.</li>
  <li><strong>Germany (ZEREZ)</strong>, <strong>UK</strong> and others — not read yet.</li>
</ul>
<p class="muted">“Listed with restrictions” and “time-limited” are the Austrian list's own status words; the other registers list without a status.
Models the Austrian list marks as not meeting the requirements are left out (we show an empty cell, never a “no”).</p>
{% endblock %}
